  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: Dataverse model-driven form XML, form web resources, PowerShell operator scripts over the Dataverse Web API, and jest tests for form scripts.</role>

  <goal>After this task:
(1) On every Main (type 2), Quick Create (type 7) and Main - Interactive experience (type 12) form of sprk_todo, sprk_event, sprk_communication and sprk_analysis, every control whose datafieldname is one of the four root columns carries disabled="true". This includes hidden controls and header controls, and covers only the columns that exist on that table. No control is removed.
(2) A user can set a root on these forms only through a filing PCF that writes the ADR-024 pair: the RegardingResolver (and, on communication forms, CommunicationConnections, which files through the same applyResolverFields path). Picking a root writes the pair naming that root, which is a direct link (rule 2 of CoreAncestorResolver.ClassifyStampSource) and is never re-stamped. Picking an intermediate makes the four columns derived copies.
(3) A record CREATED on a locked form still saves its chosen lookup and its core-ancestor stamps. The presave bridge sets the submit mode of every lookup it stages or clears to "always", so a disabled control cannot drop a staged value from the INSERT.
(4) Task 156's server rule is unchanged: the pair decides, and a root column on a filed row is a copy. A raw write made outside the forms (Web API, import, flow) is still treated as a copy and repaired by CoreAncestorStampReconciliationJob. The owner accepted this in round 8 item 3.
(5) The lock can be checked at any time with a read-only -Verify run. That run fails if a later form edit re-opens any of the controls, or adds a business rule or form library that unlocks one.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>THE COLUMN SET (task 156; read it on your base after 156 merges). `CoreAncestorResolver.CoreAncestorLookups` (src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs:107-113 on branch task/uac-r2-156-r1-r2b) names the four core-ancestor lookups: sprk_regardingproject → sprk_project, sprk_regardingmatter → sprk_matter, sprk_regardingworkassignment → sprk_workassignment, sprk_regardingservicerequest → sprk_servicerequest. `IntermediateRootColumns` (:154) gives sprk_communication, sprk_event, sprk_todo and sprk_analysis exactly these four as their root columns (StandardRootColumns). `StampSourceColumns` (:191) names the same four tables as the only tables that carry a stamp copy. The remarks at :99-106 say that a column's presence on a table is resolved from live metadata, never assumed. sprk_todo and sprk_event carry all four (live, 2026-10-01). Presence on sprk_communication and sprk_analysis is read live in step 1.

WHY THE LOCK (156 note, "Owner decision" section). When a row's pair names an intermediate (rule 3), or it has no pair and exactly one intermediate (rule 5), every root column the source can carry is treated as a copy. A root that a person types DIRECTLY onto such a row is reverted by the cascade or the job within one cycle. During that window the resolver refuses with 409 container_ancestor_stale; it never misfiles. After the repair, the row has left the secure root the person placed it under. Live exposure on 2026-10-02 was zero: all 14 to-dos filed under an intermediate carried a pair naming that source. The shape needs a raw edit of a stamp column, and the forms are the ordinary place to make one. The owner kept the rule and chose to remove that input.

NO FORM SOURCE EXISTS IN THE REPO FOR THESE FOUR TABLES (verified at authoring, 2026-10-02, case-insensitive search of every .xml file in the repo):
- The only XML files that name any of the four columns are two Matter/Project tab fragments (src/solutions/SpaarkeCore/entities/sprk_matter/FormXml/analyses/matter-analyses-tab.xml and src/solutions/SpaarkeCore/entities/sprk_project/FormXml/analyses/project-analyses-tab.xml). They are subgrids on the PARENT forms and are out of scope.
- src/solutions/SpaarkeCore/entities/sprk_todo/ holds only entity-schema.md. There is no sprk_event, sprk_communication or sprk_analysis folder there.
- src/solutions/SpaarkeCore/customizations.xml (5.9 KB) contains no form.
- src/dataverse/solutions/** (unpacked solutions) holds forms for sprk_Container only. src/dataverse/forms/** holds Matter form patches only.
- infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/AnalysisRibbons and CommunicationRibbons hold ribbon customizations only, with no form XML.
The repo's established convention for a live form edit is a Web API systemforms PATCH plus PublishXml, recorded by a checked-in script or fragment:
- matter-analyses-tab.xml's header says it was "Applied directly to the live Matter main form ... via Dataverse Web API (systemforms PATCH + PublishXml)" and that the checked-in file is the durable record of the change.
- Task 138's scripts/Retire-CommunicationAccessPermission.ps1 edits sprk_communication forms the same way.
This task therefore delivers a script, not a solution import. The live -Apply is the main session's manual gate, in place of "import the solution to dev". Customer environments receive the change through the SpaarkeMaster solution exported from dev (scripts/solution-authoring/Assemble-SpaarkeMasterSolution.ps1 exports it managed for provisioning; it maps systemforms to entities at :211-218). Whether these forms are components of SpaarkeMaster is checked in step 1 (escalation trigger 8).

THE REFERENCE SCRIPTS TO COPY.
- scripts/Retire-CommunicationAccessPermission.ps1 (task 138), for structure and the form edit:
  - comment-based help with .SYNOPSIS, .DESCRIPTION, .PARAMETER, .EXAMPLE and .NOTES, including the exit codes 0 / 2 / 1 (:1-62);
  - Get-DataverseToken through az (:87-95); Invoke-Dv with -AllowNotFound (:97-128); Write-Step / Write-Plan / Write-Done / Write-Info (:130-133); Stop-Refused, which exits 2 (:135-140);
  - the transform is a PURE string function, so a dry run shows exactly what -Apply would write (:142-155, Remove-FormReferences);
  - the workflow and business-rule scan (:189-197) and the form scan that refuses managed forms and unrecognised shapes (:199-213);
  - every write sits after the `if (-not $Apply)` exit (:297-301);
  - writes are a systemforms PATCH of formxml, then PublishXml for the table (:307-323).
- scripts/Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1, for the -Verify mode convention: `[switch]$Verify` (:73); "-Apply and -Verify are separate modes" thrown when both are passed (:80); the mode banner (:120); a VERIFY PASS that exits 0 and a VERIFY FAIL that names each gap and exits 1 (:183-191).

THE CREATE-MODE PATHS THAT A DISABLED CONTROL COULD BREAK.
- The RegardingResolver PCF is bound to sprk_regardingrecordtype, NOT to any of the four columns (src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/RegardingResolver/ControlManifest.Input.xml:3, :7). Its description names sprk_todo, sprk_event, sprk_invoice, sprk_communication and sprk_kpiassessment as host forms. sprk_analysis is NOT named (escalation trigger 1).
- The CommunicationConnections PCF (src/client/pcf/CommunicationConnections/CommunicationConnections/ControlManifest.Input.xml) is bound to sprk_associationprovenance and sprk_associationstatus and files the chosen regarding records through the shared applyResolverFields path (ResolverWriteHandler). It writes through the Web API, not through the four controls.
- UPDATE mode: the RegardingResolver writes through webApi.updateRecord (handlers/ResolverWriteHandler.ts:412, :532). That bypasses form controls, so a disabled control does not affect it.
- CREATE mode, user pick: the PCF publishes the payload on the `window.__sprk_regarding_pending__` bridge, and the presave stages it onto FORM ATTRIBUTES at OnSave (src/client/webresources/js/sprk_todo_regarding_presave.js, ns.onSave :196-345). It clears lookups first (step 2), then sets the chosen lookup (step 3), then sets each ancestor stamp (step 4), through setLookupIfPresent (:423-460) and clearLookupIfPresent (:467-488).
- CREATE mode, subgrid "+ New" auto-detect: the PCF stages the derived stamps itself with Xrm.Page.getAttribute(name).setValue (RegardingResolverApp.tsx: setFormLookupValue :789-806, setFormTextValue :809-821, the stamp loop :1250-1265) and then republishes the same stamps on the bridge so the presave re-stages them at OnSave (:1300-1318).
- CREATE mode, platform pre-fill: a "+ New" from a parent's subgrid pre-fills the parent lookup by relationship mapping (for example sprk_analysis.sprk_regardingmatter from the Matter Analyses tab, per matter-analyses-tab.xml's header). The SmartTodo "New task" launcher pre-fills sprk_regardingmatter and its siblings through form `defaultValues` parameters (src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/services/newTaskLauncher.ts:30-63, which says all catalog lookups are on the To Do main form as hidden cells). Neither path runs script on the control, and both are checked in the live gate.
- The presave's own header (:79-89) says every core-ancestor lookup must be ON the create form, hidden if need be, because getAttribute returns null for a column that is not on the form. The columns must therefore stay on the forms. This task disables the controls; it never removes them.
- The presave never calls setSubmitMode today. Whether the platform submits a value that script set on a DISABLED control is a platform detail this task does not rely on. Setting the submit mode to "always" on each lookup the presave stages makes the INSERT carry the value either way.
- The presave's jest suite drives the real script through module.exports (src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/__tests__/regardingPresave.test.ts:19). makeFormContext (:38-55) builds attributes that record setValue in call order. The test at :94-96 pins ns.VERSION to "1.3.0".
- The web resource is documented as deployed under the name sprk_/scripts/smarttodo_regarding_presave.js and registered as the form OnLoad handler Spaarke.SmartTodo.RegardingPreSave.onLoad (projects/smart-todo-r4/notes/d-form-bind-instructions.md:85, :100-104). Read the live name and registration in step 1 before relying on them.

OTHER CLIENT SURFACES THAT WRITE THE COLUMNS (found at authoring by a search of src/client and src/solutions). The shared builders (PolymorphicResolverService.buildRegardingSelectionPayload / applyResolverFields, TodoRegardingUpdateBuilder used by TodoDetail, the Create*Wizard services) write the pair together with the typed lookup. That is the direct-link shape, which the restamper never touches, so they are not the risky input. The risky input is a surface that writes a root column onto an EXISTING row without writing the pair (escalation trigger 5).

NOT A ROUTE TASK. No BFF route is in scope. RouteAuthorizationGuardTests (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs, task 074) is not touched. Task 167 has not been authored on this branch at the time of writing; whenever it lands, this task neither adds nor deletes any of its Pending waivers, because it fixes no route. ADR-003's "unknown and denied ids answer the same" has no route to apply to here; the fail-closed rules are the script's refusals and -Verify's treatment of read faults.</background>
