  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner round 8 item 3">Scope: the server rule. Do NOT change CoreAncestorResolver, CoreAncestorRestamper, CoreAncestorStampReconciliationJob or RecordContainerResolver. The owner kept the rule as shipped: the pair decides, and a root column on a filed row is a copy. Option 2 of the 156 note (the server refuses a hand-placed secure root) was NOT chosen. No file under src/server/** changes in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 8 item 3">Scope: which controls. Lock (disabled="true") every control whose datafieldname is one of the four columns, compared case-insensitively and as a whole value (FormXml can spell it sprk_RegardingMatter; sprk_regardingmatterstatus is NOT a match). This includes hidden controls (visible="false") and header controls (id prefixed "header_"). Do NOT remove any control: the presave and the PCF stage values onto these attributes on CREATE (presave header :79-89). Do NOT touch any other control. In particular, never touch the control bound to sprk_regardingrecordtype: it hosts the RegardingResolver, and disabling it disables the picker.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: which forms. Every systemform of sprk_todo, sprk_event, sprk_communication and sprk_analysis with type 2 (Main), 7 (Quick Create) or 12 (Main - Interactive experience), whatever its formactivationstate (an inactive form can be re-activated). Report, without editing, any form of another type (for example Quick View 6 or Card 11) that has a control bound to one of the four columns. Read each table's attributes live, and lock only the columns that exist on that table. A column absent on a table is reported, not treated as an error.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the transform. A PURE function over the formxml string, as Remove-FormReferences is. It edits the text of each targeted &lt;control&gt; start tag only: it adds disabled="true", or rewrites an existing disabled="false" (any case) to disabled="true", and leaves an existing disabled="true" untouched. It never re-serializes the document (no XmlDocument.Save or OuterXml round-trip), so every byte outside the targeted start tags is unchanged. After transforming, parse the result as XML: it must be well-formed, and a parsed comparison must show that no attribute changed except disabled on the targeted controls.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: the script's refusals. Fail closed. Each case below REFUSES with exit 2, names the form or component, and writes nothing:
- a managed form that has a control bound to a locked column;
- a control bound to a locked column that hosts a custom control (a controlDescription whose forControl names that control's uniqueid; confirm these attribute names against a real form read in step 1 before coding them);
- a custom control anywhere on the form that names a locked column as a bound parameter value (a PCF that could write the column through another control);
- a business rule (workflow category 2) or business process flow (category 4) on the table whose xaml or clientdata references a locked column;
- a form library whose web resource content contains a locked column name (case-insensitive) AND the token setDisabled;
- a transform result in which a control bound to a locked column is still not disabled, or that fails the parse check above;
- in -Apply, a form whose formxml changed between the scan and its PATCH (re-read it immediately before the PATCH).
In -Verify, any fault while reading forms, attributes, workflows or web resources is a FAILED check (exit 1), never "0 unlocked controls". A table that returns zero systemforms of type 2 is also a FAILED check (exit 1): a scan that sees no main form proves nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the script's modes. Copy the structure of Retire-CommunicationAccessPermission.ps1 and the mode convention of Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1. Parameters: -EnvironmentUrl (default https://spaarkedev1.crm.dynamics.com), -Apply, -Verify, -RestoreFrom path, -SelfTest, -SnapshotPath. Passing more than one of -Apply, -Verify, -RestoreFrom and -SelfTest throws before any read.
- No mode switch: a read-only dry run that prints, per form, the controls it would lock, and every refusal reason it finds.
- -Apply: run every check first. Then write the snapshot to -SnapshotPath (default: form-lock-snapshot-yyyyMMddHHmmss.json in the current directory), read the file back and parse it, and print its path. Refuse (exit 2, nothing written) if the snapshot cannot be written or read back. The snapshot records the environment URL, a UTC timestamp, and per changed form its formid, table, name, the formxml before, the formxml the script will write, and the SHA-256 of each. Then PATCH systemforms(formid) formxml, and run PublishXml once per changed table.
- -Verify: read-only. Exit 0 only when every control bound to an existing locked column on every in-scope form is disabled AND no refusal case above is present. Otherwise exit 1, naming each control or component.
- -RestoreFrom path: refuse (exit 2, nothing written) if the snapshot's environment URL differs from -EnvironmentUrl, or if any form's CURRENT formxml hash differs from the snapshot's "written" hash (the form was changed after the apply, for example by task 138's retirement script, and restoring would undo that change). Otherwise PATCH each form's "before" formxml back and publish each table.
- -SelfTest: offline, with no token and no network call. Run the pure transform and the pure refusal checks over every fixture under tests/fixtures/form-lock-core-ancestor/, print one line per case, and exit 1 on any mismatch.
- A second -Apply after a successful one reports "nothing to do" and exits 0 (idempotent).
Every Invoke-Dv call with -Method PATCH, POST or DELETE sits inside the -Apply or -RestoreFrom branch, after all checks.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: -SelfTest fixtures. Closed set, one input file and one expected-output file (or one expected-refusal file naming the refusal) per case:
(1) a visible, editable sprk_regardingmatter control gets disabled="true", and every other byte of the document is unchanged;
(2) a hidden (visible="false") sprk_regardingproject control gets disabled="true";
(3) a form with sprk_regardingworkassignment in the body AND in the header (id "header_sprk_regardingworkassignment"): both controls get disabled="true";
(4) datafieldname="sprk_RegardingServiceRequest" (mixed case) gets disabled="true";
(5) an already-disabled control is unchanged, and running the transform on the output of case 1 gives identical bytes;
(6) a control with disabled="false" becomes disabled="true", with no duplicate disabled attribute;
(7) a locked-column control that hosts a custom control is REFUSED;
(8) a custom control on another control that names sprk_regardingmatter as a bound parameter is REFUSED;
(9) NEGATIVE: controls bound to sprk_regardingrecordtype, sprk_regardingcommunication and sprk_regardingrecordname, and to a column whose name only STARTS with a locked name (a fixture-only sprk_regardingmatterstatus), are unchanged;
(10) a form with none of the four columns is unchanged and reported as nothing to do.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the presave web resource. In setLookupIfPresent and clearLookupIfPresent, after a successful setValue, call attr.setSubmitMode("always") when typeof attr.setSubmitMode is "function". Wrap that call in its own try/catch: a throw from it logs a console.warn and does NOT change the function's return value, because the value was already staged (otherwise a stamp would be logged as "not an attribute on this form", which is false). Change nothing else in their logic. Keep these unchanged: clears run before sets; the console.error on a stamp that cannot be staged; the CREATE-only gate (formType 1); the read-only skip (3 and 4); "never block the save". Do not change setAttributeIfPresent: the text fields are not in the locked set. Bump ns.VERSION to "1.4.0" and add one v1.4.0 line to the header's version history naming task 168 and the reason.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-006">Scope: client code. Create no new web resource and no new form script. The only client change is the existing presave. Do not change the RegardingResolver or CommunicationConnections PCF source. If step 1 shows that a CREATE-capable form hosting the RegardingResolver does not register the presave OnLoad handler, the PCF's own setValue would be the only CREATE staging path onto a disabled control for a user pick. That is escalation trigger 3, not a silent PCF or form-library edit.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002 / D-1">Scope: whole task. No Dataverse plugin, no plugin step, no business rule added. The lock is form configuration. The submit-mode change is in an existing form web resource.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added. Jest tests drive the real presave script through module.exports, as the existing suite does. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests. Every new guard is proven to bite by seeding: remove it, watch a named test or fixture go red, restore it byte-identical (compare SHA-256 before and after), and record the result in the task note.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project hard gate">Scope: before the PR. Run, in full, and record the counts in the note: the RegardingResolver jest suite (npm test in src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver), the full BFF unit suite (tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests), NetArchTest (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests), tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests and tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests, plus the script's -SelfTest. No Dataverse in CI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: live Dataverse during development. Read-only only: metadata reads, systemform, workflow, web resource and solution-component reads, and the script's dry run and -Verify. The executor never runs -Apply or -RestoreFrom and never deploys the web resource. Those are the main session's manual gate, in the order given in step 7.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: BFF hygiene. Not applicable: this task changes no file under src/server/**, so the publish-size and CVE checks do not apply and there is no Placement Justification to write. If the executor comes to believe a BFF change is needed, that is escalation trigger 6.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 (binding)">Scope: whole task. No scope cuts and nothing deferred; scope discovered during execution is added to this task or raised as an escalation, not pushed off. The live gate uses existing non-admin test users in their current business unit; if a gate needs a user at a specific access level, ask the owner to create one (owner round 4 item 1).</constraint>
  </constraints>

