  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Confirm that 156 is merged into your base (CoreAncestorRestamper.cs exists and the I-1 row names task 156). If it is not, STOP (escalation trigger 9). Re-verify every line anchor in the background against current source (they drift).</step>
    <step order="1">Read-only live inventory (spaarkedev1). For each of the four tables:
- which of the four columns exist (EntityDefinitions Attributes);
- every systemform (formid, name, type, formactivationstate, ismanaged, formxml);
- for each control bound to one of the columns: control id, hidden or visible, disabled now, and whether it hosts a custom control (and which);
- whether the form hosts the RegardingResolver or CommunicationConnections (a customControl named Spaarke.Controls.RegardingResolver or Spaarke.Controls.CommunicationConnections), and whether any other custom control names a locked column as a parameter;
- whether the form registers Spaarke.SmartTodo.RegardingPreSave.onLoad, and the live web-resource name of that library;
- every form library whose content references the four columns, and whether it calls setDisabled on them;
- every business rule (workflow category 2) and business process flow (category 4) for the table that references the four columns.
Also check, and record:
- whether any editable grid exposes the columns: the entity-level grid customization of each table, and subgrid controls on ANY table's forms that target one of the four tables with an editable-grid custom control;
- whether each in-scope form is a component of the SpaarkeMaster solution, either as a systemform component (componenttype 60) or through its table's entity component with all subcomponents included;
- for the text fields the bridge already stages (sprk_regardingrecordid, sprk_regardingrecordname, sprk_regardingrecordurl, sprk_regardingrecordnumber), whether any of their controls is already disabled on a CREATE-capable form, as evidence of how the platform treats script-set values on disabled controls today.
Record all of it in notes/task-168-lock-root-columns-on-forms.md, with ids shortened to their first 8 characters, and include the "no form source in the repo" evidence from the background. Stop at any escalation trigger the inventory fires.</step>
    <step order="2">Write scripts/Lock-CoreAncestorStampColumnsOnForms.ps1 by copying the reference scripts' structure. Write the pure transform and the pure refusal checks first, then the fixtures under tests/fixtures/form-lock-core-ancestor/, then -SelfTest. Make -SelfTest pass.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the dry run, -Apply (with the snapshot written and read back before any write, and the re-read before each PATCH), -Verify and -RestoreFrom (with its two refusals). Run the dry run and -Verify against spaarkedev1 (both read-only). Record their output in the note. -Verify is expected to exit 1 before the apply, and it must name each unlocked control the inventory found.</step>
    <step order="4">Presave: add the guarded setSubmitMode("always") calls and bump the version. Extend regardingPresave.test.ts: the mock attribute gets a setSubmitMode spy (and a variant whose setSubmitMode throws). Update the version test to "1.4.0". Add tests per the acceptance criteria.</step>
    <step order="5">Seed each new guard (the list is in the acceptance criteria), confirm it goes red, restore it byte-identical, and record the results.</step>
    <step order="6">Docs:
- In the I-1 row of DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md, replace only the clause "a root typed directly onto a filed row's stamp column ... (refuses meanwhile; owner decision pending, task 156 note verifier round 2 item 9)" with: the rule was confirmed by owner round 8 item 3; the four columns are read-only on the to-do, event, communication and analysis forms (task 168, checked by Lock-CoreAncestorStampColumnsOnForms.ps1 -Verify); a raw write made outside the forms is still treated as a copy and repaired by the job, which the owner accepted. Leave the row's other clauses (the AI update tool, TaskActionCore, the TS mirror, the backfill) unchanged.
- Add one "Resolved by owner round 8 item 3 (option 1 + 3) and task 168" line under the 156 note's owner-decision heading.
Then run the full test set from the hard-gate constraint.</step>
    <step order="7" mode="prescriptive">MANUAL LIVE GATE, run by the main session, in this order:
(a) confirm no other formxml-writing script (task 138's retirement script, Deploy-TodoSubgridsToElevenParentForms.ps1) is running against dev;
(b) deploy the presave web resource v1.4.0 and publish (dataverse-deploy skill), then confirm in the browser console of a to-do CREATE form that the onLoad log line names v1.4.0;
(c) run the script's dry run and review it;
(d) run -Apply and keep the snapshot path;
(e) run -Verify, which must exit 0;
(f) run the live checks in the last acceptance criterion;
(g) if any check in (f) fails, run -RestoreFrom with the snapshot, run -Verify (it should exit 1 again), and STOP (escalation trigger 7).
Step (b) comes before (d) so that no create is ever made against a disabled control with the old presave.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell. Use ✅ only after the live gate passes. Before that, use the project's completed-with-escalation convention with the live gate named as pending, and set the POML's metadata status and a status-note to match.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>1. A form a user can create or edit from (type 2, 7 or 12) exposes one of the four columns as a VISIBLE, EDITABLE control, and the form hosts neither the RegardingResolver nor CommunicationConnections. Locking that form would remove the only form input that files a record under a root. sprk_analysis is the likely case, because the RegardingResolver manifest does not name it. STOP and report the form. The owner chooses: add the RegardingResolver to that form (a separate form change), or lock it anyway.</trigger>
    <trigger>2. A control bound to one of the four columns hosts a custom control, or a custom control elsewhere on a form names one of the four columns as a bound parameter. An example is a retired PCF (such as the AssociationResolver, whose source is no longer in the repo) still placed on a live event form. Disabling the control would make that PCF read-only too, and leaving it would keep an input that writes a root. STOP and report the form, the control and the PCF.</trigger>
    <trigger>3. A CREATE-capable form that hosts the RegardingResolver does not register Spaarke.SmartTodo.RegardingPreSave.onLoad. On that form, a user pick on CREATE would have no staging path that sets the submit mode. STOP. The owner chooses: register the presave there (a form-library change), or change the PCF (version bump, rebuild, deploy).</trigger>
    <trigger>4. A form in scope is managed, or a business rule, business process flow or form library references or unlocks one of the four columns. STOP and report it. A managed layer is changed in its owning solution. An unlocking rule is product behaviour, so do not delete or edit it silently.</trigger>
    <trigger>5. A surface other than these forms lets a user write a root column onto an EXISTING row of these tables without writing the ADR-024 pair in the same write: an editable grid exposing the columns, a business process flow step, or a code page or PCF that writes them from user input outside the shared pair builders. Record every such surface in the note, then STOP. The owner's decision names the forms only, so widening the lock is the owner's call. A surface that writes the pair with the typed lookup (the shared builders named in the background) produces a direct link and does not fire this trigger.</trigger>
    <trigger>6. Any step appears to need a change under src/server/** (for example, refusing a hand-placed root on the server). That is option 2 of the 156 note, which the owner did not choose. STOP.</trigger>
    <trigger>7. The live gate shows that a CREATE on a locked form saves WITHOUT its root column or stamps: through the RegardingResolver, a "+ New" from a parent's subgrid, or the SmartTodo "New task" launcher. That is a silent under-grant (the child becomes invisible to the root's principals). The main session restores from the snapshot and STOPs. Do not ship the lock until the cause is fixed.</trigger>
    <trigger>8. The in-scope forms are not components of SpaarkeMaster (neither as systemform components nor through their table's entity component with all subcomponents). The lock would then exist in dev only. STOP and report, so the main session decides how the forms reach customers.</trigger>
    <trigger>9. Task 156 is not merged into your base. Do not branch from 156's unmerged task branch, which may still change. STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>scripts/Retire-CommunicationAccessPermission.ps1 (task 138) edits sprk_communication forms, but it REMOVES controls for a column it then deletes. scripts/Deploy-TodoSubgridsToElevenParentForms.ps1 ADDS subgrids to parent forms. scripts/Fix-DocumentFormParams.ps1, Fix-DocumentFormParams2.ps1 and Fix-AllStaleForms.ps1 repair PCF parameters. scripts/Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 verifies a role, not a form. No script or form source in the repo sets disabled on form controls, and none verifies a lock (a search of scripts/ for "disabled=" and "setDisabled" at authoring found one hit, Migrate-SecureRecordsToNamedOwnerTeam.ps1, which prints a user's isdisabled flag). No web resource in src/client/webresources or src/solutions/webresources calls setDisabled. The presave bridge already exists and is extended, not duplicated.</existing>
    <extension>The presave is extended in place (two guarded calls and a version bump). The lock script is new because no existing script has this purpose: extending the retirement script would mix a one-off column deletion with a standing, re-runnable lock, verify and restore. The new script copies the two reference scripts' helpers and mode conventions instead of inventing new ones. The fixture folder exists only so that -SelfTest can show the transform, its refusals and its idempotence offline.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A user who edits a filed to-do's Matter (or Project, or Work Assignment) lookup on the form, beside its communication regarding, places it under that root, and the job silently reverts it within 5 minutes. The child then leaves a secure root its author put it under (156 verifier round 2 item 9). Without -Verify, a later form-designer edit that re-adds or re-enables one of these controls re-opens the shape with no signal. Without the submit-mode change, a disabled control could drop a staged stamp from a CREATE, which is an under-grant. Without the guarded -RestoreFrom, a rollback after task 138's retirement run would put back a control bound to a deleted column.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

