    <output type="docs">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-156-stamp-freshness.md (one line)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-168-lock-root-columns-on-forms.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The task note holds the step-1 inventory: per table, which of the four columns exist; per in-scope form, its first-8 id, name, type, activation state and managed flag; each control bound to a locked column (id, hidden or visible, disabled now, custom-control host yes or no); whether the form hosts the RegardingResolver or CommunicationConnections and registers the presave; every business rule, business process flow and form library that references the columns; the editable-grid check; the SpaarkeMaster membership check; and the text-field evidence. It also states that the repo holds no form source for these tables, with the evidence.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The script's default run makes no write. Every Invoke-Dv call with -Method PATCH, POST or DELETE is inside the -Apply or -RestoreFrom branch, after all checks; the note lists those calls' line numbers. The dry run prints each control it would lock, per form. Passing two modes together throws before any read.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">-SelfTest exits 0, offline (no token, no network), over the ten fixture cases in the constraints. Each case behaves exactly as stated, including the refusals (7) and (8) and the NEGATIVE case (9): sprk_regardingrecordtype, sprk_regardingcommunication, sprk_regardingrecordname and the near-miss sprk_regardingmatterstatus are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeds, each one red and then restored byte-identical (SHA-256 recorded): (S1) case-sensitive matching makes fixture 4 fail; (S2) removing the custom-control-host refusal makes fixture 7 fail; (S3) removing the bound-parameter refusal makes fixture 8 fail; (S4) prefix matching (any column starting with a locked name) makes fixture 9 fail; (S5) always rewriting the disabled attribute (dropping idempotence) makes fixture 5 fail; (S6) re-serializing the document instead of editing the start tag makes fixture 1 fail; (S7) removing setSubmitMode from setLookupIfPresent makes the chosen-lookup and stamp jest tests fail; (S8) removing it from clearLookupIfPresent makes the clear jest test fail; (S9) letting a setSubmitMode throw change the return value makes the throwing-variant jest test fail; (S10) making -Verify return 0 on a read fault: run against an unreachable environment URL, it then exits 0 instead of 1; (S11) making -Verify accept a table with zero main forms: run with a deliberately wrong table filter, it then exits 0 instead of 1. Record both runs of S10 and S11 in the note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">-Verify is read-only. It exits 0 only when every control bound to an existing locked column on every in-scope form is disabled and no refusal case is present. It exits 1 naming each control or component that is not, exits 1 on any read fault, and exits 1 when a table returns zero main forms. Against spaarkedev1 before the apply, it exits 1 and names the controls the inventory found (output recorded in the note).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">-Apply writes the snapshot, reads it back and parses it before its first PATCH, and refuses with exit 2, writing nothing, if it cannot. It re-reads each form immediately before its PATCH and refuses with exit 2 if the formxml changed since the scan. It refuses with exit 2, writing nothing, on a managed form, a custom-control-hosted locked control, a custom control bound to a locked column, a business rule or business process flow referencing a locked column, a form library that unlocks one, or a transform result that leaves a locked control enabled or fails the parse check. A second -Apply reports nothing to do and exits 0. (Proven offline by -SelfTest for the pure checks, and by code reading recorded in the note for the ordering; the live proof is the gate.)</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">-RestoreFrom refuses with exit 2, writing nothing, when the snapshot's environment URL differs from -EnvironmentUrl, and when any form's current formxml hash differs from the snapshot's written hash. Otherwise it puts each snapshot's "before" formxml back and publishes each table.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Presave jest, on a CREATE form (formType 1): setSubmitMode("always") is called on the chosen lookup, on each ancestor stamp it staged, and on each lookup it cleared, each AFTER that attribute's setValue. NEGATIVE: setSubmitMode is not called for an attribute that is not on the form (getAttribute returns null); nothing is staged and setSubmitMode is never called on an UPDATE form (formType 2) or a read-only or disabled form (3, 4); the text fields in TEXT_FIELDS get no setSubmitMode call; an attribute without a setSubmitMode function is still staged and returns true; an attribute whose setSubmitMode throws is still staged, the stamp is counted as staged, and no "not an attribute on this form" console.error is logged for it. ns.VERSION is "1.4.0".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The existing presave tests pass unchanged, except the version test, which now expects "1.4.0". This includes the tests that pin clears before sets and the console.error for a stamp whose column is not on the form.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Scope check, by git diff against the base: no file under src/server/** changed; the RegardingResolver and CommunicationConnections PCF sources are unchanged; no new web resource exists; RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs is unchanged and no waiver was added or removed; no plugin was added (ADR002_PluginTests green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The I-1 row of DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md no longer says "owner decision pending" for the typed-root shape. It names owner round 8 item 3, task 168, the -Verify check, and the accepted residual (a raw write outside the forms is repaired by the job). The row's other clauses are byte-identical to the base. The 156 note carries one "Resolved" line and is otherwise unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Full runs, with counts recorded in the note: the RegardingResolver jest suite, the BFF unit suite, NetArchTest, tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests and tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests, all green, plus -SelfTest exit 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, main session, in the step-7 order), with results and first-8 ids in the task note:
(a) -Verify exits 0 after the apply.
(b) NEGATIVE: an existing non-admin test user opens each locked form type found in step 1 (Main and Quick Create for each table that has them) and cannot edit any of the four controls; each shows as locked.
(c) That user creates a to-do and picks a matter through the RegardingResolver. On read-back, the row carries sprk_regardingmatter and a pair naming the matter.
(d) That user creates a to-do and picks a communication filed under a matter. On read-back, the row carries the derived sprk_regardingmatter stamp and a pair naming the communication.
(e) A "+ New" to-do from a Matter form's To Dos subgrid saves with sprk_regardingmatter set.
(f) A "+ New" to-do from a Communication form's To Dos subgrid, where the communication is filed under a matter, saves with the derived sprk_regardingmatter stamp (the auto-detect path).
(g) The SmartTodo "New task" launched from a matter saves with sprk_regardingmatter set (the defaultValues path).
(h) Re-filing an existing to-do through the RegardingResolver (UPDATE mode) still writes the new pair and stamps.
(i) The same checks (c) and (h) on an event form, and on a communication form where step 1 found it CREATE-capable.
(j) A "+ New" analysis from a Matter form's Analyses tab, if step 1 found that path in use, saves with sprk_regardingmatter set.
If any check fails: -RestoreFrom, then escalation trigger 7.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Owner round 8 item 3 (2026-10-03) closes task 156's verifier round 2 item 9 as "option 1 + 3". Option 2 (the server refuses a hand-placed secure root) was considered and not chosen; see the first constraint.

The orchestrating brief said to change "the form definitions in source" and import the solution. At authoring, no source for these forms exists in the repo (see the background). The task follows the repo's convention for live form edits instead: a checked-in, idempotent, verifiable script, with the live -Apply as the manual gate. If the main session prefers to export these forms into source, that is a separate decision; this script's -Verify still applies afterwards.

The owner's wording names "the RegardingResolver picker". On communication forms the filing input may be CommunicationConnections, which writes the pair through the same shared path; it is treated as equivalent here (goal point 2). If the owner disagrees, that is a change to escalation trigger 1.

Not a route task. Task 167's waivers and RouteAuthorizationGuardTests are untouched.

The TypeScript stamp mirror (156 item 13a), the AI update tool's inline re-stamp (owner round 8 item 1) and the TaskActionCore pair (owner round 8 item 2) are separate tasks and are not in this task.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute; Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check are mandatory (FULL, and TEST-MODIFYING).</protocol>
    <record date="2026-10-03" branch="task/uac-r2-168" base="144b36b51">
      <rigor>FULL (security edge, live form definitions, TEST-MODIFYING). Run on Opus at effort high.</rigor>
      <inventory>Live dev, read-only: all four root columns exist on all four tables. Root controls are on these forms: to-do main eca59df4 (3, in a HIDDEN section, RegardingResolver + presave); event quick create 642e1a65 (3, hidden, no picker); event modal 90d2eff7 and Assign Work 835b8ee8 (3 each, VISIBLE, no picker); communication Message main b58ec3d8 (4, VISIBLE, no picker). Analysis forms: none. No business rules or process flows; no form library calls setDisabled; no custom control binds a root; EventAutoAssociate reads the roots but never writes them. Every in-scope form is in SpaarkeMaster (entity components with all subcomponents). The live presave is v1.2.0. Event and analysis have editable home grids.</inventory>
      <deliverables>scripts/Lock-CoreAncestorStampColumnsOnForms.ps1 (dry run, -Apply, -Verify, -RestoreFrom, -SelfTest, -Tables); tests/fixtures/form-lock-core-ancestor/ (the 10 specified cases plus 11 and 12 for triggers 1 and 3); presave v1.4.0 (forceSubmit after every staged or cleared lookup); 8 new jest tests; the I-1 row clause; the 156 note "Resolved" line; notes/task-168-lock-root-columns-on-forms.md.</deliverables>
      <deviation>Two refusals beyond the POML list, NO_FILING_PICKER (trigger 1) and PICKER_WITHOUT_PRESAVE (trigger 3), each with a fixture. A live run therefore cannot step past an owner decision. Also -Tables (needed by S11 and for a partial apply), and a read-back after -Apply that records the stored formxml for -RestoreFrom.</deviation>
      <justification>
